## Shared Web ACK ΓÇö future-stage `Waiting On` lifecycle rule

Shared Falcon Web has reviewed the Owner-directed FCR lifecycle semantics in the canonical Issue body against the current Web workstream FCR handling model.

`WEB_ACK = ACCEPTED`

No concrete incompatibility is found.

Shared Web will apply the synchronized rule going forward:

- an implementation-required FCR remains open while any owning workstream still has implementation/binding/verification work outstanding;
- future Foundation implementation work is not converted to `Waiting On: NONE` merely because its Stage/WP is future or not yet authorized;
- `Waiting On` names the immediate unresolved owning workstream, while `Target Foundation Stage/WP` and `Review Trigger` preserve future governed timing;
- completion by one owning side hands the FCR to the next owning side when another required implementation/verification obligation remains;
- planning/design/documentary acceptance does not substitute for implementation plus governed verification where implementation is required;
- FCR lifecycle state never creates implementation/runtime authority;
- historical comments/evidence remain preserved while canonical headers may be synchronized prospectively.

This ACK is a governance/process compatibility response only. It grants no Shared Web implementation/runtime/deployment authority and does not modify any Application or Foundation technical semantics.

`HANDOFF_UPDATE_REQUIRED: Waiting On=FOUNDATION; Next Required Action=Foundation shall consume the Shared Web ACK together with the corresponding Application response, then perform the planned shared FCR protocol/header synchronization or otherwise disposition the synchronization hold; Target Foundation Stage/WP=N/A ΓÇö cross-workstream FCR governance synchronization; Review Trigger=Foundation synchronization/disposition after both requested ACKs are reviewed.`
